<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy | Dare to Break Free"
  description="Information about cookies and similar technologies used on Dare to Break Free."
>
  <article class="policy-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your browser</p>
    <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="policy-page__updated">Last updated: 12 November 2026</p>

    <p>Cookies are small files stored by a website in your browser. Similar technologies can store or access information on your device.</p>

    <h2>What this website uses</h2>
    <p>The site does not currently use analytics, advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. The website code does not set cookies or use browser storage for the journaling prompt generator or other site features.</p>
    <p>The site loads fonts from Google Fonts. This makes a request to Google’s servers and shares technical connection information, but the site does not use Google Analytics or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Forms and third-party services</h2>
    <p>When you submit a form, it is sent to Formspree for processing. Formspree and the website host may use their own technical measures for security, delivery and abuse prevention. Those services operate under their own policies; their technologies are not controlled by this website. If you follow a link away from this site, the destination may also use its own cookies.</p>

    <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>You can use your browser settings to view, block or delete cookies. Blocking all cookies may affect the way some websites or third-party services work. If this site adds analytics or other non-essential cookies in future, this policy will be updated and any required choice will be offered before those cookies are used.</p>

    <p>For how personal information is handled, see the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
